+### Ewald Fourier loads at low occupancy (`ewald_fourier_loads/`)
+
+With the Fourier sum scheduled ahead of the real-space sum, its loop still
+held 14.8% of the bucket-512 adaptive kernel's stall samples with 6.9% of its
+warp instructions: 114 SASS instructions per mode, 52 of them scalar `LDC`
+(three words of the wave vector, 50 coefficients of the mode's `fourExpanse`
+row, with the row index in a vector register) and 51 `FFMA`, and the first
+accumulation after `MUFU.SIN`/`MUFU.COS` waiting for them once per mode.
+This stage takes the three follow-ups listed there in order, each measured
+against the head it was built from (`origin/main` 1bb812d0, the PC loop's
+shared-memory reads, in the same `build/arena_b1024` configuration):
+
+1. **16-byte table rows (`ldc128`).** `EwaldConstants::fourExpanse` rows are
+   padded from 82 to 84 floats (`kEwaldFourierRowStride`, a 336-byte stride)
+   and the table is declared 16-byte aligned; the generated
+   `ewaldCorrectionDerivatives` reads each mode's row through `float4` on the
+   device (`EwaldConst::fourExpansion4`, under `__CUDA_ARCH__`) and keeps
+   the scalar broadcasts on the host SIMD path. The products and their
+   summation order are unchanged on both paths.
+2. **Two modes per iteration (`unroll2`).** The generator emits the mode loop
+   two modes per iteration, both phases (`sincos`) first, so the sine and
+   cosine latency of one mode is covered by the other's accumulations; every
+   coefficient still accumulates the modes in index order (NFOUR is 92, and
+   a tail loop covers an odd count).
+3. **Warp-uniform lane loop (`uniform`).** `cudaGravityCcEwald` iterates
+   every lane to the list length rounded up to whole warps; a lane past the
+   end evaluates the last multipole's position with a zero multipole, so its
+   M2L adds exact zeros and its flops are not counted. The aim is a mode loop
+   that ptxas can prove warp-uniform, so the row addresses go to uniform
+   registers and the table reads to the uniform datapath (`ULDC`, with the
+   coefficients as uniform-register operands of the `FFMA`s).
+
+What ptxas makes of them (`sass_fourier.sh`, `loop_body.py`:
+`nvdisasm` of the order-7 kernel, the innermost loop around the first
+`MUFU.SIN`):
+
+| binary | loop body | modes per iteration | per mode: constant loads | `FFMA` | whole kernel `LDL`/`STL` |
+|---|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|
+| head | 114 | 1 | 52 `LDC` | 51 | 933 |
+| ldc128 | 177 | 2 | 25 `LDC.64` + 2 `LDC` | 51 | 934 |
+| unroll2 | 177 | 2 | 25 `LDC.64` + 2 `LDC` | 51 | 934 |
+| uniform | 177 | 2 | 25 `LDC.64` + 2 `LDC` | 51 | 923 |
+| uniform2 | 177 | 2 | 25 `LDC.64` + 2 `LDC` | 51 | 923 |
+
+Two things differ from the plan. There is no 16-byte constant load: for the
+`ld.const.v4.f32` that NVVM emits, ptxas issues two `LDC.64` (a test kernel
+reading a `__constant__` `float4` array the same way, CUDA 12.8, sm_86, gets
+the same split, as `ULDC.64` pairs even where the loop is provably uniform),
+so the 50 scalar loads of a mode become 25 two-word loads, 13 fewer
+instructions per mode than a 16-byte load would have given but half the
+load count all the same. And ptxas unrolls the `float4` loop by two on its
+own: the `ldc128` body already holds two modes, with the second mode's
+`MUFU.SIN`/`MUFU.COS` issued in the middle of the first mode's
+accumulations, and the explicit unroll of step 2 produces the same 177
+instructions in the same mix (the loop control differs by two
+instructions). The per-mode cost falls from 114 to 88.5 instructions.
+
+The warp-uniform lane loop does not reach its aim in either form, the
+rounded-up lane count (`uniform`) or the warp-wide base index whose loop
+control does not involve the lane index at all (`uniform2`): the mode loop's
+row addresses stay in vector registers (`IMAD R, R<mode>, 0x150, R<base>`),
+no `FFMA` takes a constant-bank or uniform-register operand, and the kernel's
+1,208 `ULDC`s are elsewhere (the kernel's parameters and layout). In this
+kernel ptxas promotes to uniform registers only values derived from those;
+a loop counter that starts at an immediate inside the inlined Ewald
+derivative, deep in the workitem loop, is not promoted whether or not the
+enclosing lane loop is provably uniform. The variant costs 36 selects for
+the zero multipole and 0.1% more instructions.
